# Python lint before commit

Python under `tools/`, `scripts/`, and `tests/` is linted with **Ruff** (see `pyproject.toml`).

Before **commit and push** when any of those paths changed:

1. Run `mise run lint` or `make lint` (or `mise run lint:fix` / `make lint-fix` to apply fixes, then re-run lint).
2. Do not push if lint fails — CI job **Ruff (lint + format)** in `.github/workflows/python-tests.yml` will fail the PR.

Quick reference:

- `mise run lint` / `make lint` — check only (matches CI)
- `mise run lint:fix` / `make lint-fix` — auto-fix imports and format
- `mise run check` / `make check` / `npm run corpus:check` — lint + pytest (recommended pre-push gate)

Optional local hook: `pip install pre-commit && pre-commit install` (see `.pre-commit-config.yaml`).
